## 3. Exam Tips & Trap Reminders

1. **DNS Egress Requirement**:
   When egress isolation is enabled (`policyTypes: [..., Egress]`), if the pod tries to reach a service by DNS name
   (e.g., `cache-service`), CoreDNS traffic on UDP/TCP port 53 will be dropped unless explicitly permitted!
1. **Scope of "Allow Outgoing to Pods"**:
   If an exam prompt says "allow outgoing traffic to pods" without naming a specific app label, you can use:

   ```yaml
   egress:
     - to:
         - podSelector: {}
   ```

   This permits egress to any pod inside the namespace while continuing to drop external/node traffic.
